\description{
A model geometry reads one crossvalidated geometry through a
\code{\link[=model_basis]{model_basis()}}. It lowers the plan's relation into model coordinates
(\verb{B~ = Q'B}, composing the basis with each partition's extractor),
materializes the complete compressed form \verb{S_x = Q' G_x Q} at every
measurement, and reads two fixed trace queries from the original plan.
From those it reports two things that live on different layers and are
kept apart.
}
\details{
On the \strong{signed estimation layer}, the trace decomposition
\eqn{\operatorname{tr}(H G_x H) = \operatorname{tr}(P G_x) +
\operatorname{tr}((H - P) G_x)}{tr(H G H) = tr(P G) + tr((H - P) G)}:
the centered total energy of the geometry equals its model-addressable
energy, which is \code{tr(S_x)}, plus its model-orthogonal energy. Both terms
are fixed bilinear queries with vanishing marginals, so both are unbiased
and signed, and the identity is exact at every measurement. It mirrors
\code{coherent + configuration = total} along the representational axis
instead of the spatial one.

On the \strong{latent layer}, one structure fit of \code{S_x} to the model family:
the nonnegative model-side metric \code{C} in the parameterization
\verb{G_x ~ T C T'}, with \verb{T = Q R} the stacked model factor. The four
structures are readings of one form and answer four different questions:\tabular{lll}{
   structure \tab \code{C} \tab tests \cr
   \code{isotropic} \tab one nonnegative weight per model \tab the truncated model geometries with nonnegative weights \cr
   \code{diagonal} \tab one nonnegative weight per model coordinate \tab the model axes with unequal, possibly sparse weights \cr
   \code{block} \tab one PSD rank-limited block per model \tab an independent learned metric per model (with one model, the shared fit) \cr
   \code{shared} \tab one PSD rank-limited matrix over the joint span \tab a learned readout of the joint model span, not the supplied geometries \cr
}


Only the isotropic structure tests the model geometries as supplied. The
shared fit is \code{\link[=latent_geometry]{latent_geometry()}}'s rank-budgeted truncation of \code{S_x}
(\verb{[S_x]_\{+,s\}}, the closed-form Frobenius minimizer over PSD forms of
rank at most \code{s}), not a second implementation of it. Every fit returns
\code{C} and never a factor \code{W}, because \code{W} is identified only up to rotation.
The fitted energy \code{tr(A)} and the residual \verb{||S_x - A||_F^2} are latent
quantities and are never reported as fractions of a signed denominator.
}
\section{Structure}{

One row per spatial measurement, with the estimation-layer split and the
latent-layer fit kept in separately named fields.
\itemize{
\item \verb{$addressable}, \verb{$orthogonal}, \verb{$centered_total}: the signed trace
decomposition per measurement; \verb{$identity_error} is the largest
departure of \code{addressable + orthogonal} from \code{centered_total}.
\item \verb{$fit}: a data frame per measurement with \code{residual} (Frobenius, in
model coordinates), \code{fitted_energy} (\code{tr(A)}), \code{iterations},
\code{converged} (block descent needs \code{max_sweeps} of at least two to
observe a quiet sweep unless the basis has one model), and for the
shared structure the two-part moved mass \code{clipped_negative_mass} and
\code{truncated_positive_mass}.
\item \verb{$coefficients}: the fitted \code{C}, a model-coordinate by model-coordinate
by measurement array, coordinates named \verb{<model>.<k>} as in the basis's
\verb{$R}. For \code{isotropic} and \code{diagonal}, \verb{$weights} additionally holds the
nonnegative weights per model or per coordinate.
\item \verb{$cross_fit} (with \code{training}): \code{energy} per measurement, the
per-edge energies \code{by_edge}, the \code{edges} with their weights, the
partitions each readout was trained on and how many pairing edges
trained it, the \code{rank}, the policy, and the pairing's declared
\code{independence}. It is listed under \verb{$layer$estimation}; the plug-in
\verb{$fit$fitted_energy} stays on the latent layer, and the two are never
the same number. The execution \verb{$receipt} carries none of this; its
schema is sealed.
\item \verb{$structure}, \verb{$hypothesis}, \verb{$tests_supplied_geometries}: which fit
was made and what it tests.
\item \verb{$rank}: the requested and effective budgets and whether any was
clamped.
\item \verb{$df}: \code{fit}, the free parameters of the structure, beside \code{free}, those
of the unconstrained rank-limited PSD form on \code{n - 1} centered
directions; \verb{$model_sizes} are the per-model dimensions they were
computed from.
\item \verb{$span_fraction}, \verb{$near_saturated}: the basis's span fraction and the
warning label.
\item \verb{$basis_signature}, \verb{$source_scientific_plan_id},
\verb{$lowered_scientific_plan_id}: the identities the reading was built
from; \verb{$receipt} is derived from the lowered execution.
\item \verb{$reading}: the latent reading line, which applies to \verb{$fit},
\verb{$coefficients} and \verb{$weights} and not to the trace split.
}

Any element not listed here is internal and may change.
